    <item>
      <title>Squeak 2.21.0</title>
      <pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:03:31 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>22100</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.21.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>Conductor is now an add-on you choose workspaces in: Settings › Conductor lists Conductor's workspaces with a switch each, and only the ones you add show in Squeak, in the sidebar with the Conductor mark. Nothing from Conductor shows until you add it.</li><li>Your projects can move from Conductor into Squeak, chats and folders, with <code>squeak move-from-conductor --repo &lt;name&gt;</code>.</li><li>Crash reports: after a crash, hang or force quit, the next launch sends a diagnostic report through Heresay by itself (never anything you typed).</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.20.1</h4><ul><li>The sidebar's update check is a compact icon, and pond disclosure controls are easier to click.</li><li>Resizable pane dividers have larger hit areas and show the appropriate resize cursor on hover.</li><li>Working matrix glyphs use consistent pixel sizes and softly faded edges.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.20.0</h4><ul><li>Every project is now a pond. The sidebar says Ponds, and Create says New pond.</li><li>Invite is the only step to share a pond; it signs you in first if you are signed out.</li><li>Ponds are on for everyone. A pond only you can see stays on this Mac until you invite someone.</li><li>Create opens a page in the workspace to start work, add a project or join a pond.</li><li>You can add a profile photo to your Squeak account in Settings › Account.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
